fix(research-topic): send an OpenAlex filter, not an OQL string (v0.17.0)

Found while trying to run the end-to-end acceptance on "single-image
geolocalization": the broad search returned nothing. Not degraded results —
nothing at all.

The service rendered a query and sent it as `?oql=...`. OpenAlex has no `oql`
request parameter. It answers:

    HTTP 400 — "oql is not a valid parameter. Valid parameters are: ...
    filter, search, select, ..."

So every broad search failed on the first request, and the pipeline fell
through to whatever came next. 471 backend tests stayed green because every
one of them mocks the HTTP call, so none ever checked that the parameter name
was real.

`toOpenAlexFilter` now renders the value OpenAlex actually accepts:

- `title_and_abstract.search:<term>` — the field the API documents. The
  `title/abstract has (...)` spelling in the OQL is the API's own human-facing
  rendering (it echoes something similar in `meta.x_query.oql`) and is not
  something you can send.
- `|` between terms inside one concept group (OR), the field repeated between
  groups (AND).
- `from_publication_date` / `to_publication_date` for the year window.
- No exclusions: the filter grammar has no NOT operator, so they are applied
  locally against the title instead.

That last point matters beyond this fix: exclusion terms were previously only
ever written into the OQL string, which was never sent, so they had no effect
on any run. They now do.

`OpenAlexQueryPlan` carries both forms on purpose. `oql` is readable and is
what gets archived and shown in the UI; `filter` is what goes on the wire. The
card label saying "the OQL that was actually sent" is now accurate, because
something is actually sent.

Verified against the live API: the acceptance topic returns 27 matching works,
titled things like "Distance Alignment Loss for Single Image Geolocalization"
and "A Satellite-Drone Image Cross-View Geolocalization Method".

Tests: 7 added, covering the field name, OR/AND structure, the year window,
empty groups, escaping of `,` and `|`, and that exclusions stay out of the
filter.

Verification: backend 478/478, frontend 283/283, `vite build` clean.
